PRETABLE_Q2d.corrections -- written after the 19:19:54 table (PRETABLE_Q2d.out and PREDICTIONS.* are never amended).
1. TWO PREDICTIONS WERE WRONG, and the detector is not: S7 and idata_A2_ne20 (both `writeflag == MEM_WRITE && idata !=
   0x20` at the Clear arm) were predicted GREEN and measured RED.  The new row "X14 <tk>: Clear 0x20 keeps 0x10 pending
   and enabled" writes the data 0x20 -- chosen for the drive's operands, not for this -- so the exact-value mutant
   declines that write.  Caught by VALUE, not by design.  The CONTRACT's NOT COVERED example `idata != 0x20` was
   therefore false at 864 rows; corrected (comment only) to `idata == 0` at a latched Clear write, measured green here
   (XZ_clr0), with a note that 0x20 and the irq 0x10 forms are red by value.  Instrument after that edit: 8309c5b7 --
   its code lines are identical to c187b754 (diff with comment lines removed: empty), and it re-ran 864/0 with every
   pin unchanged (pins_r3x.sh, 19:2x).
2. The analyzer's per-set tally (TABLE.txt head) lists opus / carried / closing / codexV only; the q2e (54) and extra
   (5) sets are in the per-variant lines and in the mismatch check, which covers every predicted variant: all 59 as
   predicted (28 + 0 RED as predicted, 26 + 5 GREEN as predicted).  An apparatus omission in the SUMMARY, not in the
   check.
